      "code_hash": "fc995318565e069d2ceb26ed3c2686ca",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"cloudflare-ai-use-case\">Cloudflare AI use case</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">In this notebook, we will show a simple use case using Cloudflare's\n<a href=\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/api/resources/ai/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">AI endpoints</a>.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">More information on using AI models with Cloudflare can be found here:\n<a href=\"https://ai.cloudflare.com/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">https://ai.cloudflare.com/</a></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Prerequisites:</strong><br></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">- API token (see <a href=\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/fundamentals/api/get-started/create-token/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>\nfor info on how to create one)</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "SFPL",
      "code_hash": "e5838d42e721e12b8b2a702f5af1a51d",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">In order to interact with a model using the API, it is required to specify the model on the endpoint URL,\nas well as model specific inputs as the json payload.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">For a complete list of all models available, as well as their inputs, see the dedicated\n<a href=\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers-ai/models/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">developers webpage</a>.\nEach model also has simple usage snippets to help users get started. Here we will present two model\ninteractions:</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "RGSE",
      "code_hash": "f97ea88d888e35cc5df772b0a29dcad0",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h3 id=\"text-generation-example\">Text generation example</h3>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Using the <code>@cf/meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct</code> model, we will ask the model for information about Workers AI.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "emfo",
      "code_hash": "3faa317d3c8b7c166ae87024fa05f20a",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h3 id=\"translation-example\">Translation example</h3>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Now changing to the <code>@cf/meta/m2m100-1.2b</code> model, we will translate a portuguese sentence into english.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "nWHF",
      "code_hash": "277cb1dc1c328ff3bfb48b322bd116a7",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"checking-ai-model-usage\">Checking AI model usage</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The Cloudflare dash has a page dedicated to account level AI model usage, which can be found in the\n<code>AI tab &gt; Workers AI</code> page.\nAlternatively, we can perform queries using GraphQL to obtain the same information. Let's fetch the\nmost used models in the last 30 days.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">These metrics are measured in number of neurons used, which represent GPU usage.\nFor more information, including neuron usage per model, check the\n<a href=\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers-ai/platform/pricing/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">AI platform pricing page</a>.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Vxnm",
      "code_hash": "765681249b121489605ef96bbca1dccf",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><b style='color: tomato'>Note:</b> Since we are querying for the current day, results may be incomplete.\nNot only that, but if this query is executed right after running the prompt above, model usage may not be\nupdated in time.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "DnEU",
      "code_hash": "a0b947b8f589b93e074afb52bc951469",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"going-further\">Going further</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">We can take advantage of Cloudflare's tooling to unlock more advanced use cases. One such example involves\nusing R2 buckets, which can act as storage to both model inputs and outputs.\nTo see more on R2 interactions, check the <code>r2</code> example notebook.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
